      "id": 1791287692971.8696,
      "question": "The 5th term of an arithmetic progression is 18 and the common difference is 3. What is the first term?",
      "options": [
        "6",
        "9",
        "12",
        "15"
      ],
      "correctAnswer": 0,
      "explanation": "Let the first term be a. The nth term of an AP is T<sub>n</sub> = a + (n − 1)d. For n = 5: a + 4d = 18 ⇒ a + 4(3) = 18 ⇒ a + 12 = 18 ⇒ a = 6.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
    {
