      "correctAnswer": 1,
      "explanation": "T<sub>n</sub> = S<sub>n</sub> − S<sub>n−1</sub>. S<sub>n</sub> = 3n<sup>2</sup> + 2n. S<sub>n−1</sub> = 3(n − 1)<sup>2</sup> + 2(n − 1) = 3n<sup>2</sup> − 4n + 1. Thus T<sub>n</sub> = (3n<sup>2</sup> + 2n) − (3n<sup>2</sup> − 4n + 1) = 6n − 1. T<sub>10</sub> = 6(10) − 1 = 59.",
      "difficulty": "easy",
      "points": 1
    },
